{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MassSideKernelFormalizeFirstGates","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MassSideKernelFormalizeFirstGates","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_direction_threshold_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_direction_threshold_positive","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L299-L304","doc":"**Threshold positivity helper**: the direction threshold is > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_reject_anchor_too_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_reject_anchor_too_large","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L286-L297","doc":"**Rejection: failing the §4(a) gate prevents bundle instantiation.**\n\nConcrete rejection lemma for the most common failure mode\n(cross-anchor swing too large). Analogous rejection lemmas exist\nper-field via the parametric gate classes above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.massSideKernel_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.massSideKernel_iff","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L254-L284","doc":"**The bundle IS the conjunction of its gates** — the `.md`'s\n*\"instantiating `MassSideKernel` requires clearing all four mass-side\ngates simultaneously\"*, stated as an equivalence.\n\nAdded 2026-08-31 (bean `qou-z9ws`). The three lifting lemmas above are the\n**forward** half and nothing more: each returns the inherited field its\ntype restates, which is the accessor idiom (`Group.mul_assoc`), not a\nderivation. The converse — that holding the three gate instances suffices\nto build the bundle — was never stated, so the block's actual claim, an\nequivalence, had no Lean. It does now.\n\n§4(b), the bar-even invariant, is deliberately not a parent class here (it\nis the Q_β `CommRing R` structural identity and holds for any kernel), so\n\"all four gates\" is these three plus that external one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_implies_q_one_shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_implies_q_one_shadow","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L244-L251","doc":"**§4(c) lifting (when registered)**: from the bundle with a\nregistered anchor, the q=1 shadow holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_implies_direction_sanity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_implies_direction_sanity","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L235-L242","doc":"**§4(d) lifting**: from the bundle, the direction-sanity gate holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_implies_anchor_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_side_kernel_implies_anchor_stable","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L227-L233","doc":"**§4(a) lifting**: from the bundle, the anchor-stability gate holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.toMassQOneShadowGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.toMassQOneShadowGateClass","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L219-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.toMassDirectionSanityGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.toMassDirectionSanityGateClass","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L219-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.toMassAnchorStableGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel.toMassAnchorStableGateClass","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L219-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassSideKernel","kind":"class","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L203-L223","doc":"**`MassSideKernel` — the unified mass-side formalize-first typeclass.**\n\nParametric over the four candidate-specific values:\n- `w`: the candidate linking_weight function\n- `swing`: cross-anchor swing magnitude (probe-computed)\n- `anchor`: registered q=1 categorical anchor (None for open gap)\n- `magnitude`: |w(q_0)| substrate magnitude\n\nDefined as the extension of the three per-gate parametric classes\nthus the bundle equals the conjunction of its parents by construction.\nMirrors the decay-side `BarEvenKernel` typeclass; uses the\n`extends` pattern for cleaner downstream composition.\n\nThe §4(b) bar-even invariant is automatic for substrate-derived\ncandidates via the Q_β CommRing R lemma (PR #1875). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates","label":"prop:mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_direction_sanity_reject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_direction_sanity_reject","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L184-L194","doc":"**Gate theorem (refute, §4(d)):** if the magnitude exceeds the\nthreshold, the class cannot be instantiated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_direction_sanity_forward","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_direction_sanity_forward","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L174-L182","doc":"**Gate theorem (forward, §4(d)):** under the class, the magnitude\nis bounded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassDirectionSanityGateClass.magnitude_within_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassDirectionSanityGateClass.magnitude_within_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L170-L170","doc":"Additive bound: |m_candidate - target| ≤ threshold · target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassDirectionSanityGateClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassDirectionSanityGateClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L168-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassDirectionSanityGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassDirectionSanityGateClass","kind":"class","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L152-L172","doc":"**§4(d) mass-side direction-sanity gate.**\n\nParametric over the candidate's substrate magnitude\n`m_candidate = |w(q_0)|`. Instantiation requires\n`|m_candidate - target| ≤ threshold · target` — the additive\nform that matches PR #1890's `q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean`\nLean precedent.\n\nNote: sympy probes (e.g. `mass_theory_formalize_first_invariants_probe.py`,\nPR #1896) implement the multiplicative variant\n`max(|m|/target, target/|m|) ≤ threshold` for the operational\ndirection-magnitude check; the additive form here is the Lean-\nside abstract scaffold that admits both variants as instances\n(a multiplicative-passing candidate also satisfies the additive\nform within the same threshold magnitude). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_q_one_shadow_reject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_q_one_shadow_reject","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L143-L150","doc":"**Gate theorem (refute, §4(c)):** if a registered anchor exists\nand the candidate's q=1 limit disagrees, the class is rejected. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_q_one_shadow_forward","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_q_one_shadow_forward","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L134-L141","doc":"**Gate theorem (forward, §4(c)):** under the class with a\nregistered anchor, the candidate's q=1 limit matches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassQOneShadowGateClass.shadow_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassQOneShadowGateClass.shadow_holds","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L132-L132","doc":"The candidate's q=1 limit matches the registered anchor (when\none exists). Vacuously true when `anchor = none`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassQOneShadowGateClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassQOneShadowGateClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassQOneShadowGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassQOneShadowGateClass","kind":"class","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L109-L132","doc":"**§4(c) mass-side q=1 classical-limit shadow gate.**\n\nParametric over the candidate `linking_weight` function w AND the\nregistered anchor (Option ℝ). The anchor is `Option` because the\nregistered categorical value for linking_weight(q=1) is the OPEN\nGAP identified by PR #1896 — no canonical derivation exists yet.\n\nThe field is stated as `∀ a, anchor = some a → w 1 = a` rather\nthan a `match`-on-type to keep the class fully Prop-valued without\nrelying on iota reduction in user-facing theorems. When\n`anchor = none` this is vacuously true; when `anchor = some a` it\nrequires `w 1 = a`.\n\nThis enables FUTURE candidates (e.g. PR #1899's Σ f^λ/4 = 5/2\nfinding = #involutions(S_4)/4) to be evaluated against the\nhypothetical anchor `some (5/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_anchor_stable_reject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_anchor_stable_reject","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L100-L107","doc":"**Gate theorem (refute, §4(a)):** if the swing exceeds the\ntolerance, the class cannot be instantiated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_anchor_stable_forward","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.mass_anchor_stable_forward","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L92-L98","doc":"**Gate theorem (forward, §4(a)):** under the class, the swing is\nbounded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassAnchorStableGateClass.swing_within_tolerance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassAnchorStableGateClass.swing_within_tolerance","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The candidate's cross-anchor swing is within the 1 ppm\nfibre-level tolerance (PR #1727). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassAnchorStableGateClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassAnchorStableGateClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassAnchorStableGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.MassAnchorStableGateClass","kind":"class","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L79-L90","doc":"**§4(a) mass-side anchor-stability gate.**\n\nParametric over the cross-anchor swing magnitude `swing` (typically\ncomputed by a sympy probe as `|w(q_μ) - w(q_p)| / |w(q_p)|`).\nInstantiation requires the swing to be within the 1 ppm fibre-level\ntolerance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.directionThreshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.directionThreshold","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L67-L69","doc":"Direction-sanity threshold (10× order-of-magnitude check). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.directionTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.directionTarget","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L62-L65","doc":"Direction-sanity target for `linking_weight` at q_0 (CODATA-implied\nnear-match ≈ 2.46 per PR #1850 framing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.anchorTolerance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.anchorTolerance","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L58-L60","doc":"Anchor-stability tolerance (1 ppm relative, per PR #1727 fibre-level). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.q_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MassSideKernelFormalize.q_substrate","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-side-kernel-formalize-first-gates.lean#L54-L56","doc":"The proton-pinned substrate q_0 (50 dps). ","signatureChunk":0}]}